ially it quote does not participate  in sanctions against russia  but the reality is although it may do so  very quietly it does participate  no chinese bank no matter how patriotic  is willing to risk defying american  sanctions  likewise in 2021 china passed an  anti-sanctions law which essentially  makes it illegal for chinese nationals  to comply with american sanctions  against china  make no mistake this law is driven not  by supreme confidence but rather  deep-seated fear  if sanctions were nothing to worry about  it wouldn't be necessary  its purpose is to increase the cost of  sanctions thereby in theory making them  less likely  but this reluctance goes both ways  that divide between saying and doing is  also quite large in america  trade is of course a two-way street  chinese imports mean dollars in the bank  for american companies  not to mention that many chinese imports  are then assembled into final products  and shipped to the states  this is a list of companies on the smp  with the highest percentage of sales in  china  with the sole exception of wynn resorts  which operates casinos in macau  nine of the top 10 are suppliers of  semiconductors or other advanced  technology components  not far behind with one fourth of its  revenue coming from china is the second  largest public company on earth by  market cap apple  if the american semiconductor industry  were cut off completely from china it  would lose at least 80 billion dollars  and 125 000 jobs according to the  commerce department  beyond lost sales these companies rely  on china to reach their economies of  scale  if they lost half their unit sales you  can expect they'd be less than half as  competitive therefore globally  such an extreme move would mean the end  of u.s dominance over the highest of  high tech  taken as a whole american companies have  around 400 billion dollars at risk in  china  decoupling as it's often called would  lower american gdp by an estimated two  percent  chinese